Here’s a compact, prioritized checklist of things to research and add into your supplier/product search and broader go‑to‑market work for each site.

High‑priority (applies to both)
1. Top product categories — SKU list with variants (size/color/model).  
2. Target unit price, MSRP, and margin target (wholesale, MAP, affiliate rates).  
3. MOQ and sample availability.  
4. Lead times (production + shipping) and shipping costs to key markets.  
5. Certifications & compliance (CE/FCC/UL, CPSIA, REACH, FDA, ISO).  
6. Packaging format and private‑label options (retail-ready, bulk, inserts).  
7. Minimum order quantities for branded vs. plain products.  
8. Return, warranty, and after‑sales support terms.  
9. Supplier reliability: references, factory audit, photos, QC process.  
10. SKU master data: weights, dimensions, HS codes, materials, power specs.

DealInstinct (general deals / bargain shopping)
1. High‑velocity deal categories: electronics accessories, household gadgets, kitchen tools, pet supplies, travel gear.  
2. Price tiers for “everyday deals” vs “flash deals” vs “premium offers.”  
3. Fast‑turn items (low MOQ, quick shipping) for frequent promotions.  
4. Bundling opportunities and curated gift sets.  
5. Clearance / overstocks sources and liquidation suppliers.  
6. Affiliate programs & coupon partnerships to augment supplier deals.  
7. Return/refund policies that support frequent promotions.  
8. Product imagery and short video clips for deal creatives.  
9. P&L per deal: landed cost, promo margin, expected conversion rate.  
10. Sourcing filters: cheap replicable goods vs differentiated products.

BikerInstinct (cycling & outdoor)
1. Core categories: helmets, lights, locks, apparel, gloves, saddles, pedals, bike tools, pumps, panniers, bike computers.  
2. Technical specs to capture: material (carbon/aluminum), weight, waterproof/IP rating, lumens, battery type, cadence/speed sensors, compatibility standards (e.g., Shimano SPD).  
3. Safety certifications (CE EN1078, CPSC) and materials testing.  
4. Sizing charts (apparel, helmets) and fit guides.  
5. Performance indicators: weight, stiffness, battery life, lumens, range.  
6. Accessory bundling (light + mount, pump + patch kit).  
7. OEM/ODM possibilities for branded lines and limited runs.  
8. Seasonal items vs evergreen items (training vs commuter).  
9. Influencer/athlete samples and review units policy.  
10. Warranty/repair center options and spare parts availability.

Commercial & SEO/marketing intel
1. Keyword demand and CPC for priority SKUs.  
2. Top competitors and price benchmarking.  
3. Best converting product page elements (reviews, spec tables, comparison).  
4. Content topics and long‑form guides for organic traffic.  
5. Email lead magnets, funnels, and post‑purchase flows.  
6. Affiliate commission structure and coupon strategy.  
7. CRO experiments: urgency, scarcity, social proof placements.  
8. PPC landing page templates per category.  
9. UGC/review acquisition process and moderation rules.  
10. Analytics tags and KPIs to track per SKU (CTR, CR, AOV, return rate).

Operational/logistics
1. Fulfillment options: FBA, 3PL, dropship, MCF.  
2. Customs, HS codes, duties, and VAT implications for top countries.  
3. Insurance, lot traceability, and batch testing for safety items.  
4. Forecasting model inputs: seasonality, promo calendar, lead time.  
5. Packaging sustainability options and labeling laws.

